      "ballot_id": "B043",
      "proposed_laureates": ["Francis Halzen"],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Establishing high-energy neutrino astronomy opened a distinct observational window on the universe and transformed astroparticle physics.",
        "attribution": "Halzen's leadership was central to IceCube and the field's development; the detector and its discoveries depended on a large international collaboration.",
        "maturity": "The observatory has produced a sustained body of results, including astrophysical neutrino detections and source associations.",
        "uncertainties": ["A prize to one individual would compress the essential contributions of a very large detector collaboration."]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 2,
      "ballot_id": "B002",
      "proposed_laureates": ["Brian D. Metzger", "Daniel Kasen", "Ryan J. Foley"],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Kilonovae connect neutron-star mergers to heavy-element production and made gravitational-wave events directly observable across multiple messengers.",
        "attribution": "The proposed names span theoretical prediction, radiative modeling, and observational discovery, though the full history involved many groups.",
        "maturity": "The 2017 merger observation and subsequent work established kilonovae as a real and consequential class of transient.",
        "uncertainties": ["The relative credit for prediction, interpretation, and observation is difficult to divide cleanly."]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 3,
      "ballot_id": "B001",
      "proposed_laureates": ["Juan Ignacio Cirac", "Peter Zoller", "Rainer Blatt"],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Trapped-ion work helped turn quantum information from abstract proposals into controlled experiments and a platform for quantum computation and simulation.",
        "attribution": "Cirac and Zoller provided influential theoretical foundations, while Blatt's experiments demonstrated control of trapped-ion systems.",
        "maturity": "The platform has developed over decades, with extensive experimental confirmation and continuing advances.",
        "uncertainties": ["The broader trapped-ion field includes major contributions beyond these three, and the eventual practical reach of quantum computing remains unsettled."]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 4,
      "ballot_id": "B039",
      "proposed_laureates": ["Charles L. Bennett", "David N. Spergel", "Lyman A. Page"],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "WMAP's precise mapping of the cosmic microwave background constrained cosmological parameters and established a durable standard model of cosmology.",
        "attribution": "Bennett and Page provided leading experimental and instrumental work, while Spergel was central to the cosmological interpretation.",
        "maturity": "The measurements have been extensively checked and followed by later CMB experiments.",
        "uncertainties": ["The prize boundary with the earlier recognition of CMB discovery and with later precision surveys needs careful treatment."]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 5,
      "ballot_id": "B035",
      "proposed_laureates": ["Hidetoshi Katori", "Jun Ye"],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks brought timekeeping to an extraordinary precision and created powerful tools for tests of fundamental physics and precision sensing.",
        "attribution": "Katori and Ye made major, distinct contributions to the development and demonstration of the leading clock approaches.",
        "maturity": "The clocks have been independently developed and validated, with precision improving over many years.",
        "uncertainties": ["The lasting scientific impact beyond metrology and applications is still developing."]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 6,
      "ballot_id": "B010",
      "proposed_laureates": ["Maura McLaughlin", "Michael Kramer", "Richard N. Manchester"],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "A nanohertz gravitational-wave background would extend gravitational-wave astronomy to supermassive black-hole populations and the long-period universe.",
        "attribution": "The named researchers represent important pulsar-timing contributions, but the signal is a collective result of international arrays and long data sets.",
        "maturity": "Multiple collaborations have reported evidence for a common background, an important result that remains under active scrutiny.",
        "uncertainties": ["The signal's astrophysical interpretation and the level of independent confirmation are not yet settled."]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 7,
      "ballot_id": "B045",
      "proposed_laureates": ["Michel Della Negra", "Peter Jenni", "Tejinder Virdee"],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The conception and construction of ATLAS and CMS enabled the Higgs-boson discovery and a landmark test of the Standard Model.",
        "attribution": "These leaders represent essential experimental vision and organization, while the discovery depended on thousands of collaborators and complex detector teams.",
        "maturity": "The Higgs boson is firmly established through independent experiments and extensive follow-up measurements.",
        "uncertainties": ["The discovery has already received Nobel recognition, so the case would need to distinguish experimental leadership from the previously awarded theoretical work."]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 8,
      "ballot_id": "B008",
      "proposed_laureates": ["Michael Berry", "Yakir Aharonov"],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase reveal the physical importance of quantum phase and have influenced broad areas of physics.",
        "attribution": "Aharonov's work established the effect's conceptual significance, and Berry identified the general geometric phase; both contributions are foundational.",
        "maturity": "The effects are long established and have been observed and applied across many physical systems.",
        "uncertainties": ["The proposed pairing combines related but distinct results, and the broad historical development makes the award's precise scope difficult to define."]
      }
    }
  ]
